*Experiment 4 -> To study and execute their process management commands and use Vim and Nano text editors for creating, editing and managing text files in Ubuntu Linux*

*Procedure: Process Management command ->*
1) Open terminal in ubuntu
2) Check running process -> ps
3) Display all running process -> ps aux
4) Continuously monitor processes -> top
5) Find a process by name - pgrep process_name
6) Terminate a process - kill PID
7) Run a process in the background -> command &
8) View background jobs -> jobs

*(B) Using Nano Editor -*
1) Create /open a file -> nano http://test.txt
2) Type some text
3) Press Ctrl + O -> Enter to save
4) Press Ctrl + X to exit

*(C) Using Vi Editor:*
1) Create / Open a file -> vi http://test.txt
2) Type some text
3) Type your text and Press Esc
4) Type -> :wq and Press Enter to Save and Exit

*Result ->* Successfully Executed linux process management commands and use Vi and Nano editor to create, edit, save and manage text files in ubuntu linux
